rengths: reliability, stress, technical. Weaknesses: communication tone, pretentiousness may affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: can anticipate dangerous situations (stress resilience, decision quality), sees complex connections (technical), excellent spatial vision (technical), very good leadership (crew cooperation), but unfriendly, eats unhealthily (maybe health, but not directly criteria). Strengths: anticipation, technical, leadership. Weaknesses: unfriendly (crew cooperation), unhealthy (maybe reliability). No mention of stress handling directly but anticipation suggests.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but considered moody, regarded as a loner (crew cooperation). Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, concentration. Weaknesses: moodiness, loner (cooperation).\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely B has strong reliability and stress, but communication issues. C has strong technical and leadership but unfriendly. D has responsibility and problem solving but moody. A has quick decisions and concern for others but egocentric and poor communication.\n\nWhich candidate balances? B seems strong on reliability and stress, technical, but communication tone could be mitigated? C's unfriendly may be serious for crew cooperation. D's moodiness could affect long flights. A's egocentric may be problematic.\n\nThus B might be best overall despite communication concerns. Let's propose B as current recommendation, citing strengths and acknowledging concerns.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: none, but we can say \"Given the initial overview\". Provide facts: B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, but pretentious and wrong tone. Explain that strengths outweigh concerns.\n\nThus vote for Candidate B.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
